# trucks.bug

> Module: truck_tracking (Kamyon Takip) | Category: FLEET  
> Last Tested: 02 June 2026

---

### B-TRK-01: Truck PUT Returns 404 With Extra Fields

| Field | Detail |
|-------|--------|
| **Severity** | P2 — Medium |
| **Status** | ⬜ **OPEN** |
| **Found** | API testing — `PUT /api/tenant/trucks/{id}` with full body returns 404 |
| **Reproduced** | `PUT /api/tenant/trucks/6` with body `{"id":6,"plaka":"06 BUG 2222","marka":"Test","model":"Bug","yil":2025,"tracking_source":"GPS_CIHAZ","yakit_tipi":"DIZEL","aktif":true}` → `{"success":false,"error":"truck not found"}` (404) |
| **Working case** | Same ID with `{"plaka":"06 BUG 2222","marka":"Updated","yil":2025}` → 200 (successful update) |
| **Bug** | The truck update handler rejects PUT requests that include fields the handler doesn't expect to be mutable (`id`, `aktif`, `tracking_source`, `yakit_tipi`). The error message "truck not found" is misleading — the truck exists (confirmed by DELETE returning 200 for same ID). The real issue is that the handler can't parse or refuses to update certain fields. |
| **Impact** | Frontend might send the full truck object (all fields) on update, causing the PUT to fail. Users get a confusing "not found" error when the truck clearly exists. |
| **Root Cause** | The handler's UPDATE SQL statement may not handle all columns from the request body. If the JSON body includes `id` or `aktif`, the handler may fail to parse or bind correctly. |
| **Required Fix** | 1) Make the handler accept (and ignore) `id` in PUT body since frontend may send the full object. 2) Allow updating `tracking_source` and `yakit_tipi` via PUT. 3) Fix error message to say "invalid update data" instead of "truck not found". |
| **Files to Change** | `backend/internal/handlers/trucks.go` |
| **CI Gate to Add** | `api-smoke`: verify truck PUT works with full object (all fields from GET response) |

### B-TRK-02: Truck POST Field Validation — `yakit_tipi` Not Accepted

| Field | Detail |
|-------|--------|
| **Severity** | P3 — Low |
| **Status** | ⬜ **OPEN** |
| **Found** | Test showed that sending `"yakit_tipi":"DIZEL"` in POST body doesn't fail but the field may not be persisted. |
| **Bug** | The truck handler's POST endpoint accepts `yakit_tipi` in the JSON body but the `trucks` table schema may not have a `yakit_tipi` column or the handler doesn't bind it. The frontend FuelLogPage sends this field expecting it to be stored. |
| **Impact** | Fuel type information silently lost on truck creation. |
| **Required Fix** | Verify schema has `yakit_tipi` column on `trucks` table, or accept it and store it. |
| **CI Gate** | Schema check in `module-consistency` job |
